# SECURITY: SSH private keys must NEVER be committed to version control
# 
# This file previously contained a committed SSH private key which created
# a critical security vulnerability allowing unauthorized access to EC2 instances.
#
# The private key has been removed. SSH keys should be:
# 1. Generated outside of the repository
# 2. Stored securely (e.g., AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault)
# 3. Provided to Terraform via environment variables or secure parameter stores
# 4. Never committed to version control or stored in plain text
#
# For deployment, provide the SSH public key via the 'ssh_public_key' variable
# in terraform/modules/webserver/main.tf

